From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:18:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07681/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5830: goal-hypothesis
 verifier (the goal verifier the winner recipe lacks)

The winner-recipe reproduction showed gemma-4-31B induces WRONG goals
(fluent hypothesizer, no verifier). This is Carnot's verification-first
thesis. GoalVerifier falsifies a goal against the ONLY ground-truth
win signal a hidden-game agent legitimately observes -- the level
counter: a goal pursued with real frame-changing activity for
goal_patience actions with ZERO level-ups is FALSIFIED and fed back so
the model must hypothesize a DIFFERENT win condition. Oracle-DISTINCT
(verifier_is_oracle=False): never reads the win predicate, only
whether a level-up happened (the reward signal, not the win
definition). Wired into run_greedy_direct(goal_verify=True), fed into
reflection + decision prompts. --goal-verify on the driver.

New module + 12 tests; spec REQ-ARC-WMTE-5830 + 2 scenarios; 22
greedy-direct tests still green; mypy clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
